## Why This Is Asked

This scenario tests knowledge of vector DB usage, chunking strategy, latency, and graceful fallback in a realistic but beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation
- Document chunking
- Embedding models
- Vector DB indexing and search
- Latency targets and freshness
- Fallback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple chunker
function chunkText(text, maxChars) {
  const chunks = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += maxChars) {
    chunks.push(text.slice(i, i + maxChars));
  }
  return chunks;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle overlapping chunks to preserve context?
- How would you test latency and accuracy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design skills for production AI systems, understanding of trade-offs between accuracy and latency, and knowledge of evaluation metrics in real-world scenarios.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates will discuss: 1) Multi-stage evaluation architecture, 2) Confidence threshold tuning, 3) Fallback strategies, 4) Monitoring and alerting, 5) Cost optimization through early filtering.

## Code Example
```typescript
class HallucinationDetector {
  async evaluate(response: string, context: string) {
    const semanticScore = await this.semanticCheck(response, context);
    if (semanticScore > 0.9) return { confident: true, score: semanticScore };

    const factualScore = await this.factualVerification(response);
    const ensembleScore = this.ensembleWeighting(semanticScore, factualScore);

    return {
      confident: ensembleScore > 0.85,
      score: ensembleScore,
      needsReview: ensembleScore < 0.7
    };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle edge cases where the knowledge graph is incomplete?
- What metrics would you track to optimize the confidence thresholds?
- How would you design A/B testing for new detection algorithms?

## Why This Is Asked
To evaluate ability to design end-to-end retrieval systems with multilingual data, latency constraints, and production-grade maintenance. The candidate must articulate chunking, embeddings, indexing, reranking, provenance, and monitoring trade-offs in a realistic enterprise setting.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-augmented generation
- Embeddings for multilingual data
- Vector databases and indexing strategies (IVF+PQ, HNSW)
- Document chunking and provenance
- Reranking with cross-encoders
- Drifts, updates, caching, latency budgets
- Evaluation metrics: recall@k, QA accuracy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: initial retrieval then rerank
function retrieveAnswer(query, docs){
  const chunks = chunkDocs(docs);
  const emb = embed(query);
  const candidates = vectorDB.search(emb, topK=10);
  const ranked = reranker.rank(query, candidates);
  return formatAnswer(ranked[0]);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor embedding drift across languages?
- How would you handle adding a new language with few examples?
- What metrics would you use to balance latency vs. accuracy?

